# Run artifacts — transcripts, raw scanner output, benchmark traces
runs/
# The retention tombstone ledger (agents-dm8n): local, append-only, per-VM state
# explaining every removal under runs/; lives at the root so clearing runs/ cannot take it
/retention-ledger.jsonl
schedules/*.plist
schedules/*.service
schedules/*.timer

# Sensitive findings data (vulnerabilities, candidate tokens, target threat models, run history)
findings/*
!findings/.gitkeep
!findings/suppressions.yaml

# Never commit credentials. The factory holds high-value secrets by design.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Local engine state
.agent-state/
# The root package.json is a pi-package manifest with NO dependencies, so a root lockfile locks an
# empty tree: it carries no information and any npm command in this checkout recreates it. It has
# already reached a branch by accident once (agents-fy26) and turned up in two reviewer worktrees
# the same day. Scoped to the root deliberately - if this package ever declares a real dependency,
# delete this rule so its lockfile can be committed.
/package-lock.json
# Fast-gate scratch suites (agents-xawg): tests/test_fast_gate_mapping.py writes a probe test into tests/
# for the duration of a gate run, because the gate has to RUN it, and removes it in a `finally`. A suite that
# the gate's own bound KILLS leaves the probe behind, and a lane committing with `git add -A` would then land
# a stray test nobody owns. Ignoring the pattern is the load-bearing half; setUpClass in that suite also
# clears any leftover, so the leak heals on the next run.
tests/test_*_probe_tmp.py

# Staged Pages artifact (tools/stage_site.py) — build output, never committed
_site/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
